cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Variant Calling: Hands-on Training"
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Arun
    family-names: Seetharam
    email: aseethar@purdue.edu
    affiliation: >-
      Rosen Center for Advanced Computing,
      Purdue University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6789-9298"
# TBD(P10): other authors.
repository-code: "https://github.com/rcac-bioinformatics/variant-calling"
url: "https://rcac-bioinformatics.github.io/variant-calling"
abstract: >-
  A hands-on Carpentries-style workshop on calling germline
  SNVs and small indels from Illumina short-read data on an
  HPC cluster. Using the Genome in a Bottle Ashkenazi trio
  (HG002, HG003, HG004) on GRCh38, the lesson covers read
  quality control, alignment with bwa mem, joint calling with
  bcftools, filtering and benchmarking against GIAB truth sets,
  annotation with SnpEff and gnomAD frequencies, and a trio
  analysis of candidate de novo and recessive variants.
keywords:
  - variant-calling
  - snv
  - indel
  - vcf
  - bcftools
  - samtools
  - bwa
  - giab
  - trio
